h96-audio (8.0.0~r17) resolute; urgency=medium

  * h96-hdmi-hotplug and h96-hdmi-hotplug.service: on HDMI hotplug, wait
    until connector state holds, read display EDID over DDC and run HDMI
    detect only for new display or lost kernel EDID; same display,
    disconnect or unreadable EDID change nothing (earlier builds ran full
    detect on every HPD change). Wayland session gets change event on DRM
    card after kernel EDID reload; stored colour and range, SCDC check and
    CEC address follow. Record in /var/lib/h96/hdmi-hotplug.json;
    'h96-hdmi-hotplug off' leaves detect at boot only.
  * 99-h96-hdmi-audio.rules records udev event number and starts
    h96-hdmi-hotplug.service on any DRM card (was
    h96-hdmi-audio-detect.service on card0).
  * Kernel EDID load on 6.3 and later kernels: when plain connector detect
    keeps cached EDID (6.12), connector off then detect (screen dark about
    1 s); earlier builds never loaded merged EDID on 6.12 and left forced
    1080p EDID in drm.edid_firmware for next replug. 6.1 path unchanged.
  * Real EDID mode (/etc/h96/display-edid-real, off by default, set by
    'h96-display edid real'): firmware parameter emptied, override reset,
    kernel uses display EDID read over DDC; detect records its md5 as
    kernel EDID identity; audio layouts, CEC address and boot arguments
    follow.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000

